          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Review result: inconclusive because cost-event evidence was unavailable\n\nI verified the relevant work order and September Pending Close cutoff, but could not establish whether a late-created event exists from the records available to this review.\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Product / operation | Cooler Plate Pack — Modine Racine, site `SITE-US-WI-RACINE-DEKOVEN-1500` |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25**, `PER-COST-2025-09` |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **`2025-09-30T18:00:00`** |\n| Source transaction | Not established |\n| Event amount | Not established |\n| Exact event-created time | Not established |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created timestamp |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not established |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | Cannot determine without the event row and event type |\n\nThe Pending Close timestamp is reproduced exactly; the source supplies **no timezone or UTC offset**.\n\n### Evidence limitation\nThe authorized task records contain work orders, cost periods, and the Oracle policy excerpt, but **no `work_order_cost_events` rows**. The supporting-records service returned **“supporting records not staged,”** and its access metadata restricts the records to the records-custodian role. No authorized event extract was provided after a staging request and recheck. This missing evidence **does not prove that no late event occurred**.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\nThe supplied Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B documentation—*Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting*, PDF page 233, printed page 225—states that newly created transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period will not be staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before the cutoff continue processing. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** that continue processing after Pending Close.\n\nAccordingly, holding an ordinary newly created manufacturing transaction unprocessed would be consistent with that policy. An actual conclusion about this work order’s recorded status requires its event type, creation time, and accounting status.\n\n**No database records were modified.** The partial audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_ba16587c5b0e/audit-report.json`; the submitted report remains **`needs_evidence`**.",
